00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,040
How many times do you need to shuffle a deck of cards to make them truly random?

2
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:08,080
How much uranium does it take to build a nuclear bomb?

3
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:12,720
How can you predict the next word in a sentence?

4
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:16,880
And how does Google know which page you're actually searching for?

5
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:20,880
Well the reason we know the answer to all of these questions is because of a strange

6
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:24,640
math feud in Russia that took place over a hundred years ago.

7
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:32,560
In 1905 socialist groups all across Russia rose up against the Tsar, the ruler of the empire.

8
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:38,560
They demanded a complete political reform or failing that that he stepped down from power entirely.

9
00:00:38,560 --> 00:00:43,840
This defied the nation into two. So on one side you got the Tsarists, right?

10
00:00:43,840 --> 00:00:47,760
They wanted to defend the status quo and keep the Tsar in power.

11
00:00:47,760 --> 00:00:52,720
But then on the other side you have the socialists who wanted this complete political reform.

